sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: TCP handshake and two independent byte streams
  accDescr: Client sends SYN with sequence 100. Server sends SYN ACK with sequence 300 and acknowledgment 101. Client acknowledges 301. After establishment, three client bytes advance the server acknowledgment to 104, two server bytes advance the client acknowledgment to 303. Transport acknowledgments do not establish application consumption or business completion.
  participant C as Client TCP
  participant S as Server TCP
  C->>S: SYN seq=100
  S->>C: SYN + ACK<br/>seq=300, ack=101
  C->>S: ACK seq=101, ack=301
  Note over C,S: ESTABLISHED at both ends
  C->>S: 3 bytes: seq=101
  S->>C: ACK ack=104
  Note over C,S: ACK = next byte expected<br/>Application may not have read it
  S->>C: 2 bytes: seq=301
  C->>S: ACK ack=303
  Note over C,S: Independent byte sequences<br/>Business completion is separate
